==English==

===Etymology===
From the expression ''the [[early bird catches the worm]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-early bird.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[person]] who [[wake]]s [[early]] or [[arrive]]s early, typically before most others.
#: {{syn|en|early riser|morning person|lark}}
#: {{ant|en|nighthawk|night owl|night person|late riser}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1974|author=w:Shel Silverstein|chapter='''Early Bird'''|title=[[w:Where the Sidewalk Ends (book)|Where the Sidewalk Ends]]|publisher=HarperCollins
|passage=If you’re a bird, be an '''early bird'''— But if you’re a worm, sleep late.}}

